  ],
  "sections": {
    "overview": "<div class=\"mb-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-2 border-l-4 border-primary pl-3\">1. Executive Summary</h2><p class=\"text-on-surface-variant text-lg\">This section outlines the critical changes in Google's developer ecosystem with the release of Antigravity 2.0. It serves as an urgent briefing on why migrating from v1.0 is not optional, but essential for resource management and system security.</p></div><div class=\"box-error p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm mb-8\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-4\"><span style=\"font-size: 2rem; margin-right: var(--space-md);\">🚨</span><div><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-2\">Critical Token Depletion Warning</h3><p class=\"text-on-surface mb-3\">If you do not upgrade to Antigravity 2.0, the legacy v1.0 client will consume your entire weekly token allocation in a matter of hours.</p><p class=\"text-sm text-on-surface-variant interactive-box p-3 rounded\" style=\"background-color: var(--surface-container-low);\"><strong>Why?</strong> The older version lacks the new Delta-Sync capability. Every time an agent prompts the LLM, v1.0 re-uploads your entire project context. Antigravity 2.0 utilizes local intelligence to only send structural pointers and delta changes.</p></div></div></div><div class=\"interactive-grid grid-3\"><div class=\"interactive-box p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm\"><div style=\"font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);\">🚀</div><h4 class=\"font-bold text-on-surface mb-2\">Paradigm Shift</h4><p class=\"text-sm text-on-surface-variant\">Moving from monolithic, sequential agents to decentralized, high-speed swarm architectures.</p></div><div class=\"interactive-box p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm\"><div style=\"font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);\">🛡️</div><h4 class=\"font-bold text-on-surface mb-2\">Total Isolation</h4><p class=\"text-sm text-on-surface-variant\">Transitioning to a portable, sandboxed execution model, eliminating OS-level dependency conflicts.</p></div><div class=\"interactive-box p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm\"><div style=\"font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);\">📉</div><h4 class=\"font-bold text-on-surface mb-2\">85% Cost Reduction</h4><p class=\"text-sm text-on-surface-variant\">Implementation of cloud Context Caching drastically reduces repeated token processing costs.</p></div></div>",
    "models": "<div class=\"mb-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-2 border-l-4 border-primary pl-3\">2. Gemini 3.5 Flash vs 3.1 Pro</h2><p class=\"text-on-surface-variant text-lg\">Understanding the distinct capabilities of the new model lineup is crucial for defining agent behavior. This section analyzes the performance metrics and explains the counter-intuitive credit consumption rate of the Flash model.</p></div><div class=\"interactive-box p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm mb-8\" style=\"background-color: var(--surface-container-low);\"><h3 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-on-surface mb-4 text-center\">Capability Matrix Comparison</h3><div class=\"chart-container\" style=\"height: 350px;\"><canvas id=\"modelRadarChart\"></canvas></div></div><div class=\"interactive-grid\"><div class=\"interactive-box p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between\" style=\"background-color: var(--surface-container-low);\"><div><div style=\"font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);\">🧠</div><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4\">Gemini 3.1 Pro</h3><ul class=\"space-y-3\" style=\"list-style-type: none; padding: 0;\"><li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span style=\"color: var(--primary);\">✔</span><div><strong class=\"block text-on-surface\">Deep Reasoning</strong><span class=\"text-sm text-on-surface-variant\">Excels in complex, multi-step logical deduction and architecture planning.</span></div></li><li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span style=\"color: var(--primary);\">✔</span><div><strong class=\"block text-on-surface\">Context Window</strong><span class=\"text-sm text-on-surface-variant\">4M Tokens limits, designed for massive, single-shot contextual analysis.</span></div></li><li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span style=\"color: var(--primary);\">✔</span><div><strong class=\"block text-on-surface\">Execution Pace</strong><span class=\"text-sm text-on-surface-variant\">Slower, deliberate outputs prioritizing accuracy over speed.</span></div></li></ul></div></div><div class=\"interactive-box p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between\" style=\"background-color: var(--surface-container-low); border-color: var(--primary);\"><div><div style=\"font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);\">⚡</div><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4\">Gemini 3.5 Flash</h3><ul class=\"space-y-3\" style=\"list-style-type: none; padding: 0;\"><li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span style=\"color: var(--tertiary);\">✔</span><div><strong class=\"block text-on-surface\">Rapid Iteration</strong><span class=\"text-sm text-on-surface-variant\">Near-instant responses, ideal for high-frequency agentic loops and sub-tasks.</span></div></li><li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span style=\"color: var(--tertiary);\">✔</span><div><strong class=\"block text-on-surface\">Extended Limits</strong><span class=\"text-sm text-on-surface-variant\">8M Tokens limit to support endless micro-interactions within a session.</span></div></li><li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span style=\"color: var(--warning);\">⚠️</span><div><strong class=\"block text-warning\">The Credit Burn Paradox</strong><span class=\"text-sm text-on-surface-variant\">Although cheaper per token, its immense speed causes agents to execute hundreds of operations per minute. Without strict throttling, Flash 3.5 accelerates credit consumption simply through sheer throughput.</span></div></li></ul></div></div></div>",
    "architecture": "<div class=\"mb-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-2 border-l-4 border-primary pl-3\">3. Architectural Shifts: Hub & Workspaces</h2><p class=\"text-on-surface-variant text-lg\">This section explores the structural evolution from the legacy Agent Manager to the decentralized Agent Hub v2.0, alongside the new methodology for handling multi-repository projects without physical merging.</p></div><div class=\"mb-12\"><h3 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6\">Agent Management Evolution</h3><div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4 mb-6\" style=\"display: flex; gap: var(--space-md); margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);\"><button id=\"btn-old-mgr\" class=\"interactive-box text-on-surface-variant\" style=\"flex: 1; padding: var(--space-md); border-radius: var(--radius-md); font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; text-align: center; border: 1px solid var(--outline); transition: all 0.2s;\">v1.0 Agent Manager</button><button id=\"btn-new-hub\" class=\"interactive-box text-on-surface\" style=\"flex: 1; padding: var(--space-md); border-radius: var(--radius-md); font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; text-align: center; border: 1px solid var(--outline); background-color: var(--primary-container); color: var(--primary); transition: all 0.2s;\">v2.0 Agent Hub</button></div><div id=\"arch-display\" class=\"interactive-box p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm min-h-[250px] transition-all duration-300\" style=\"background-color: var(--surface-container-low); padding: var(--space-lg); border-radius: var(--radius-xl);\"><div id=\"content-new-hub\" class=\"block\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-4 mb-4\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-md); margin-bottom: var(--space-md);\"><div class=\"w-12 h-12 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-2xl\" style=\"background-color: var(--primary-container); width: 3rem; height: 3rem; border-radius: 50%;\">🌐</div><h4 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface\" style=\"margin: 0;\">Agent Hub (v2.0)</h4></div><p class=\"text-on-surface-variant mb-4\">A decentralized swarm architecture designed for parallel processing.</p><ul class=\"interactive-grid\" style=\"list-style-type: none; padding: 0;\"><li class=\"interactive-box p-4 rounded-lg\"><strong class=\"block text-on-surface\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);\">Real-time Sockets</strong>Agent-to-agent communication happens via high-speed WebSockets, bypassing the main execution thread.</li><li class=\"interactive-box p-4 rounded-lg\"><strong class=\"block text-on-surface\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);\">Visual Debugging</strong>Built-in visual node graphs allow developers to trace logic paths across multiple active agents in real-time.</li><li class=\"interactive-box p-4 rounded-lg\"><strong class=\"block text-on-surface\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);\">Swarm Protocol</strong>Agents can dynamically spawn sub-agents based on task complexity without centralized bottlenecking.</li></ul></div><div id=\"content-old-mgr\" class=\"hidden\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-4 mb-4\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-md); margin-bottom: var(--space-md);\"><div class=\"w-12 h-12 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-2xl\" style=\"background-color: var(--outline-variant); width: 3rem; height: 3rem; border-radius: 50%;\">📦</div><h4 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface-variant\" style=\"margin: 0;\">Agent Manager (v1.0)</h4></div><p class=\"text-on-surface-variant mb-4\">The legacy system relied on a monolithic, sequential execution loop.</p><ul class=\"interactive-grid\" style=\"list-style-type: none; padding: 0; opacity: 0.7;\"><li class=\"interactive-box p-4 rounded-lg\"><strong class=\"block\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);\">Sequential Queue</strong>Tasks were queued and executed one by one, creating massive bottlenecks on complex prompts.</li><li class=\"interactive-box p-4 rounded-lg\"><strong class=\"block\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);\">Black-box Execution</strong>Tracing agent logic required parsing through thousands of lines of raw text logs.</li><li class=\"interactive-box p-4 rounded-lg\"><strong class=\"block\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);\">Centralized Failure</strong>A failure in the manager loop would crash all subordinate agent tasks instantly.</li></ul></div></div></div><div class=\"interactive-box p-8 text-on-surface shadow-xl\" style=\"background-color: var(--surface-container-lowest); border-radius: var(--radius-xl); border: 1px solid var(--outline);\"><h3 class=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-4 flex items-center gap-3\"><span style=\"font-size: 2rem; margin-right: var(--space-sm);\">📂</span> Multi-Repo Virtualization</h3><p class=\"text-on-surface-variant mb-6\">Antigravity 2.0 solves the fragmented microservices problem. Instead of physically merging repositories to provide context to Gemini, you now define virtual workspaces using <code style=\"background-color: var(--surface-container-high); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font-family: monospace; color: var(--tertiary);\">antigravity.yaml</code>.</p><pre style=\"background-color: var(--surface-container-low); padding: var(--space-md); border-radius: var(--radius-md); font-family: monospace; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant); color: var(--on-surface);\">\nworkspace:\n  name: \"global-ecommerce\"\n  repositories:\n    - path: \"../frontend-react\"\n      alias: \"@ui\"\n    - path: \"../backend-go\"\n      alias: \"@api\"\n    - path: \"../database-schemas\"\n      alias: \"@db\"\n  context_rules:\n    - share_types: true\n  </pre><p class=\"text-sm text-on-surface-variant mt-4\">This configuration maps local paths to a unified virtual cloud environment. The AI can seamlessly cross-reference a React component in <code style=\"color: var(--primary);\">@ui</code> with the corresponding Go handler in <code style=\"color: var(--primary);\">@api</code> as if they were in a single folder.</p></div>",
    "performance": "<div class=\"mb-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-2 border-l-4 border-primary pl-3\">4. Performance & Security</h2><p class=\"text-on-surface-variant text-lg\">Examine the mechanisms behind the dramatic 85% token reduction and the architectural reasoning behind moving from system-level installations to portable, sandboxed environments.</p></div><div class=\"interactive-grid\"><div class=\"interactive-box p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm\" style=\"background-color: var(--surface-container-low);\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-2 flex items-center gap-2\"><span style=\"color: var(--primary); margin-right: var(--space-xs);\">🧠</span> Local Intelligence & Caching</h3><p class=\"text-on-surface-variant mb-6 text-sm\">The v2.0 application uses a small local model to build a semantic index of your workspace. When prompting, it only sends the <strong>delta (changes)</strong> and pointers to the cloud, utilizing the new Context Caching API.</p><div class=\"chart-container\" style=\"height: 250px;\"><canvas id=\"tokenChart\"></canvas></div></div><div class=\"interactive-box p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-center\" style=\"background-color: var(--surface-container-low);\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4 flex items-center gap-2\"><span style=\"color: var(--tertiary); margin-right: var(--space-xs);\">🛡️</span> The Chromium Sandbox</h3><p class=\"text-on-surface mb-4\">Google removed the classic installer in favor of a portable folder approach. Why? <strong>Agentic safety and dependency hell.</strong></p><ul class=\"space-y-3\" style=\"list-style-type: none; padding: 0;\"><li class=\"flex gap-3\" style=\"display: flex; gap: var(--space-sm); margin-bottom: var(--space-md);\"><div style=\"background-color: var(--surface-container); width: 1.5rem; height: 1.5rem; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: bold; flex-shrink: 0; color: var(--primary);\">1</div><p class=\"text-sm text-on-surface-variant\"><strong>V8 Isolation:</strong> The portable app runs agent generated code within a Chromium-based sandbox, preventing malicious or buggy code from accessing your host OS.</p></li><li class=\"flex gap-3\" style=\"display: flex; gap: var(--space-sm);\"><div style=\"background-color: var(--surface-container); width: 1.5rem; height: 1.5rem; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: bold; flex-shrink: 0; color: var(--primary);\">2</div><p class=\"text-sm text-on-surface-variant\"><strong>No APT Conflicts:</strong> It uses OS-level execution isolation (cgroups/namespaces). It ships with its own dependencies, never conflicting with your system's Node or Python versions.</p></li></ul></div></div>",
    "migration": "<div class=\"mb-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-2 border-l-4 border-primary pl-3\">5. Linux Migration Guide</h2><p class=\"text-on-surface-variant text-lg\">Due to the shift away from standard system repositories, a clean manual update is required on Linux. Follow this interactive guide to purge the old installation and deploy the v2.0 portable sandbox.</p></div><div class=\"interactive-box rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl\" style=\"background-color: #1e1e1e; border: 1px solid var(--outline); padding: 0;\"><div class=\"border-b\" style=\"background-color: #2d2d2d; padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md); border-color: var(--outline); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;\"><div style=\"display: flex; gap: var(--space-xs);\"><div style=\"width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #ef4444;\"></div><div style=\"width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #f59e0b;\"></div><div style=\"width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #10b981;\"></div></div><div style=\"font-family: monospace; font-size: var(--text-xs); color: #94a3b8;\">bash - step <span id=\"step-counter\">1</span> of 3</div></div><div style=\"padding: var(--space-lg); font-family: monospace; font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: 1.7; min-height: 180px;\"><div id=\"step-1\" class=\"terminal-step block\"><p style=\"color: #4edea3; margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);\"># Step 1: Purge the old APT repository and installation</p><p style=\"color: #f1f5f9; margin-bottom: 2px;\">$ sudo apt-get purge antigravity-agent</p><p style=\"color: #f1f5f9; margin-bottom: 2px;\">$ sudo rm /etc/apt/sources.list.d/google-antigravity.list</p><p style=\"color: #f1f5f9; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);\">$ sudo apt-get update</p><div style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-size: var(--text-xs); margin-top: var(--space-md);\">This ensures the legacy v1.0 manager is entirely removed from your system variables.</div></div><div id=\"step-2\" class=\"terminal-step hidden\"><p style=\"color: #4edea3; margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);\"># Step 2: Download and extract the portable sandbox</p><p style=\"color: #f1f5f9; margin-bottom: 2px;\">$ curl -O https://dl.google.com/antigravity/v2.0/ag-linux-x64.tar.gz</p><p style=\"color: #f1f5f9; margin-bottom: 2px;\">$ tar -xzf ag-linux-x64.tar.gz -C ~/development/</p><p style=\"color: #f1f5f9; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);\">$ cd ~/development/antigravity-2.0</p><div style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-size: var(--text-xs); margin-top: var(--space-md);\">The portable format contains all isolated V8 engine dependencies.</div></div><div id=\"step-3\" class=\"terminal-step hidden\"><p style=\"color: #4edea3; margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);\"># Step 3: Execute the sandbox environment</p><p style=\"color: #f1f5f9; margin-bottom: 2px;\">$ chmod +x antigravity-sandbox</p><p style=\"color: #f1f5f9; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);\">$ ./antigravity-sandbox --init-workspace</p><div class=\"box-warning p-3 rounded\" style=\"font-size: var(--text-xs); margin-top: var(--space-md); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-sm); border: 1px solid var(--warning); background-color: rgba(253, 230, 138, 0.05);\"><span style=\"font-size: 1.2rem;\">⚠️</span><span style=\"color: var(--on-surface);\"><strong>Revert Process:</strong> If needed, simply delete the folder. No system uninstallation required.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"border-t\" style=\"background-color: #2d2d2d; padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg); border-color: var(--outline); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;\"><button id=\"btn-prev-step\" class=\"interactive-box\" style=\"padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font-weight: 500; font-size: var(--text-sm); border: 1px solid var(--outline); cursor: pointer; color: #94a3b8; transition: all 0.2s;\" disabled>← Previous</button><div style=\"display: flex; gap: var(--space-xs);\" id=\"step-indicators\"><div style=\"width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: var(--primary);\"></div><div style=\"width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: var(--outline);\"></div><div style=\"width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: var(--outline);\"></div></div><button id=\"btn-next-step\" class=\"interactive-box\" style=\"padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--text-sm); border: 1px solid var(--outline); background-color: var(--primary-container); color: var(--primary); cursor: pointer; transition: all 0.2s;\">Next Step →</button></div></div>"
  },
